        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[[xhr] xhr.abort is inaccurate]]></title>
            <link>https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/23961</link>
            <guid>https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/23961</guid>
            <pubDate>Sun, 29 Jan 2023 01:52:09 GMT</pubDate>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3 dir="auto">MDN URL</h3>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/XMLHttpRequest/abort" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/XMLHttpRequest/abort</a></p>
<h3 dir="auto">What specific section or headline is this issue about?</h3>
<p dir="auto"><em>No response</em></p>
<h3 dir="auto">What information was incorrect, unhelpful, or incomplete?</h3>
<p dir="auto">"The XMLHttpRequest.abort() method aborts the request if it has already been sent. When a request is aborted, its <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/XMLHttpRequest/readyState" rel="nofollow">readyState</a> is changed to XMLHttpRequest.UNSENT (0) and the request's <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/XMLHttpRequest/status" rel="nofollow">status</a> code is set to 0."</p>
<h3 dir="auto">What did you expect to see?</h3>
<p dir="auto">Compare to the spec, it's clear that this doesn't cover the second case:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">If <a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" rel="nofollow">this</a>’s <a href="https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-xmlhttprequest-state" rel="nofollow">state</a> is opened with <a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" rel="nofollow">this</a>’s <a href="https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#send-flag" rel="nofollow">send() flag</a> set, headers received, or loading, then run the <a href="https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#request-error-steps" rel="nofollow">request error steps</a> for <a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" rel="nofollow">this</a> and <a href="https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#event-xhr-abort" rel="nofollow">abort</a>.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3 dir="auto">Do you have any supporting links, references, or citations?</h3>
<p dir="auto"><em>No response</em></p>
<h3 dir="auto">Do you have anything more you want to share?</h3>
<p dir="auto"><em>No response</em></p>]]></content:encoded>
